Z||000002||Raydar||05-06-2001||03:33 PM||||This has been tossed around for a long time. <BR>I know of at least one that was in the works.<BR>A 4.3 is a complicated swap. It requires a tranny adapter, like a Chevy V-8. It also requires mounts to be fabricated. A 3.8 is much more bang for the buck.<BR>Try searching "4.3". <P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
