Z||000004||fierogt88||05-06-2001||08:36 PM||||more bang for the buck?? hmmm....<P>I'm working on a plan for a 4.3 swap.  You might get more bang for the buck when comparing a 3800 __supercharged__ to a 4.3,  but not with your plane-jane 3.8.<P>but since I'm going 4.3 __supercharged__...  well, let's just say I think everyone here will be pleasantly surprised.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Raydar||05-06-2001||11:58 PM||||Well, somebody had to be the pioneer. Please pass along info about progress, etc. <BR>Pics would be nice, too.<BR>(As much of a pain in the ass as this swap appears to be, I still think it would be cool.)<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||14
Z||000006||erikred||05-07-2001||12:27 AM||||I considered this myself. 4.3 can be built alot. The swap should be similar to a v8 swap only with more room at the front of the engine. It is a 350 missing two cylinders. Many parts enterchange. My dad had a regular 4.3 in his astro, that engine felt pretty powerful compared to the 3.8 powered cars I have driven.<P>Erik-||||reg||14
Z||000007||Raydar||05-07-2001||09:54 AM||||I've got a 4.3 in my 92 Sonoma. It's the TBI version, not the CPI. It makes tons of torque. Enough to have broken two motor mounts.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>It only makes about 160-170 HP, though. One other thing to consider. The earlier 4.3s -the ones without the balance shaft- vibrate like hell, at around 3000-3500 RPM. (Guessing. don't have a tach.) <BR>If you use solid mounts, it might be uncomfortable in the car.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<P>88 black Formula<BR>88 soon-to-be-V6 coupe||||reg||1
Z||000008||Carrolles||05-07-2001||11:15 AM||||I have a 94 Safari with the enhanced 4.3 (200 hp) and it pulls the van along very nicely.  I think it would make a Fiero really go.||||reg||1
Z||000009||NPlack||05-07-2001||01:53 PM||||I have also wondered the same about the 4.3.  I had originally considered a 2.8/3.1/3.4 swap, but they are expensive to work with as far as performance.  Also, if I do a swap, I will be going twin-turbo.  Then the 4.3 makes much more sense.  I can use forged pistons from a 350, and not spend a fortune to have them made for the 60 degree motor, and all the other parts on this motor are the same.  4.3's and SBC's are a dime a dozen.  Also, teh 4.3 has MUCH more potential than the 60's.  More reliable i beleive.<P>-Plack||||reg||1
