Z||000012||fierogt88||05-07-2001||03:50 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Mr.Frosty:<BR><B>If you slap a Vortec turbo\supercharger onto that,then wouldn't that technically be a Syclone\Typhoon setup or motor? <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Absolutely.  The Syclone/Typhoon is turbo.  It uses an "older" version of the 4.3 (the one with the vib problems, i believe).  I will be using a 96+ Vortec motor with a supercharger.  The 4.3 swap will be this winter, the supercharger the next.  I'll be at the Carlisle show this year, with the express intention of researching all the variables of using a V8Archie setup.  I would be suprised if I didn't run into somebody with a 4.3 setup while I'm there.  I'll be looking for a 2 wheel drive S10/Blazer in the boneyards for the donor.  I should be able to squeeze 200 HP out of the first round, and should get 300 HP (or close) after the supercharger.||||reg||1
Z||000013||mshill||05-07-2001||03:56 PM||||What type of Supercharger for the 4.3 are you  considering?  I have a 4.3 with TBI in my boat and a 4.3 TPI in my 94 Safari van (blows smoke on startup, leaky valve seals).  I would like to put a SC on my boat and if it worked out swap one into a fiero as well.  The 4.3's are really easy to work on too.||||reg||1
